<div class="info-page terms-page" style="max-width: 860px; margin: var(--space-8) auto; padding: 0 var(--space-4);">
  <article class="card" style="padding: var(--space-6); border: var(--border-thick); border-radius: var(--radius-md); background: var(--color-surface-card);">
    <h1 style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--font-size-2xl); margin-bottom: var(--space-2);">Terms of Use</h1>
    <p style="font-size: var(--font-size-sm); color: var(--color-ink-muted); margin-bottom: var(--space-6);">Private beta · Version <code><%= termsVersion %></code> · Updated 21 October 2026</p>
    <h2>1. Who runs The Vinyl Drop</h2>
    <p>The Vinyl Drop is a free, invite-only community website for vinyl collectors, run by Jaap Hopman as a private individual. Privacy and service questions can be sent to <a href="mailto:<%= contactEmail %>"><%= contactEmail %></a>. The service is currently a small, non-commercial pilot; legal and provider details are described in the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Notice</a>.</p>
    <h2>2. Who may use the pilot</h2>
    <p>The initial pilot is restricted to people who are at least 18 years old and have been invited. During this early test, features and data may change while bugs are fixed. Do not create an account or use the service if you are under 18 or have not been authorized to join the pilot.</p>
    <h2>3. Accounts and access</h2>
    <p>Provide accurate account information, keep sign-in details secure, and contact the project if you believe your account has been accessed without permission. Google OAuth test-user eligibility and the application's private-beta access check are separate controls; passing one does not guarantee access through the other.</p>
    <h2>4. Listings and user-to-user arrangements</h2>
    <p>The site helps users publish and discover records offered for sale or trade. Buyer and seller are responsible for checking item details, deciding whether to proceed, agreeing on price or trade, and arranging collection or other logistics. The Vinyl Drop does not process payments, provide escrow, arrange shipping, or guarantee that another user will perform an agreement.</p>
    <h2>5. Your content</h2>
    <p>You are responsible for the listings, photos, profile details, comments and other content you submit. Submit only content you have rights to use, keep descriptions honest, and do not publish another person's private information. You retain ownership of your content and give The Vinyl Drop limited permission to host, process and display it as needed to operate the service and show it to the audience you chose, such as visitors to a published listing.</p>
    <h2>6. Community Rules and moderation</h2>
    <p>The <a href="/community-rules">Community Rules</a> supplement these Terms. We may hide or remove content, or restrict access, where reasonably necessary to address safety, abuse, fraud, legal requests, security incidents, or a breach of these Terms or the Community Rules. To report a listing, comment, suspected illegal content, fraud or an account/security concern, use the <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>. Reports and requests to review a moderation action are handled manually during the pilot; the service does not offer automated moderation appeals.</p>
    <h2>7. Beta availability and third-party services</h2>
    <p>The service is experimental and may be interrupted, contain errors, or change. Catalog lookup and sign-in may use third-party services under their own terms and privacy practices. The Vinyl Drop does not guarantee the accuracy or continued availability of externally sourced catalog information.</p>
    <h2>8. Privacy and requests</h2>
    <p>The <a href="/privacy">Privacy Notice</a> describes the information the application handles, the providers used and the current request process. Contact <a href="mailto:<%= contactEmail %>"><%= contactEmail %></a> for access, correction or deletion requests. Account deletion and export are not currently self-service; requests are handled manually. The Privacy Notice explains the limits around provider retention, automatic deletion and data recovery.</p>
    <h2>9. Suspension and changes</h2>
    <p>We may suspend or end pilot access where reasonably needed to protect people, the service or its data, or where these Terms are breached. These Terms may change during the beta. Material updates will identify the current version so users can review the Terms before continuing.</p>
    <h2>10. Applicable law and mandatory rights</h2>
    <p>These Terms are intended to be governed by the laws of the Netherlands, subject to any mandatory rules that apply to the user in their circumstances. Nothing in these Terms excludes or limits rights or liability that cannot lawfully be excluded or limited.</p>
